WEBVTT

00:49.507 --> 00:50.717
Stand back!

00:50.800 --> 00:52.802
It's dangerous! Please step back!

00:52.886 --> 00:53.803
What's the damage?

00:53.887 --> 00:55.597
Oh, Inspector Nakamura.

00:55.680 --> 00:56.848
You won't believe it.

00:57.599 --> 01:01.853
A localized tornado is one thing,
but for it to only damage a single truck?

01:02.395 --> 01:06.274
And, of all things,
an animal transportation truck, right?

01:06.357 --> 01:07.358
Yes, sir.

01:07.442 --> 01:10.403
Lions, tigers, and cheetahs. Five in all.

01:10.487 --> 01:11.654
What?

01:11.738 --> 01:13.823
We've got a problem, Inspector Nakamura!

01:15.116 --> 01:15.950
A child!

01:25.794 --> 01:27.378
Can't we do something?

01:27.462 --> 01:30.632
A rescue team in the area is on standby,

01:31.132 --> 01:33.885
but all five cats must be taken out
all at once or else...

01:34.427 --> 01:37.222
Damn it! Call for more sharpshooters!

01:37.972 --> 01:38.807
What is it?

01:38.890 --> 01:41.768
A little girl has crossed the police line!

01:41.851 --> 01:43.478
What is she doing?

01:48.066 --> 01:49.400
Don't be scared.

01:49.484 --> 01:51.903
It's all right. Come here, everyone.

01:57.659 --> 02:01.037
That's right. Nothing to be afraid of.

02:21.266 --> 02:22.267
Now!

02:26.229 --> 02:27.397
We've secured the boy.

02:28.606 --> 02:29.649
Hey now!

02:29.732 --> 02:32.610
You're scaring them with those guns!

02:36.573 --> 02:37.532
It's Uran!

02:38.116 --> 02:39.492
Give me a break.

02:42.871 --> 02:45.039
You sensed that they were afraid?

02:45.623 --> 02:46.457
Yes.

02:46.541 --> 02:48.626
So let me get this straight, Uran.

02:49.127 --> 02:51.921
You're saying
the lion and the tigers were afraid?

02:54.215 --> 02:56.301
I don't know. I guess.

02:56.926 --> 03:02.891
And that's why you walked two miles
out of your way to school to go there?

03:02.974 --> 03:04.017
Yeah, so?

03:04.100 --> 03:08.021
You can sense that animals are afraid
from that far away?

03:09.647 --> 03:10.481
Yeah, I guess.

03:12.233 --> 03:13.234
Wow.

03:13.318 --> 03:14.694
What an amazing ability.

03:14.777 --> 03:15.653
So...

03:17.155 --> 03:18.698
Can I go now?

03:23.244 --> 03:24.078
Oh!

03:24.913 --> 03:28.917
I'm sorry for all the trouble
my sister has caused, Inspector Nakamura.

03:29.000 --> 03:32.378
Oh, not at all.
She's actually been a huge help.

03:32.462 --> 03:38.259
Exactly. Thanks to me, the big cats
calmed down, and the boy was saved.

03:39.802 --> 03:41.763
Worthy of
the Superintendent General Award.

03:41.846 --> 03:44.766
I don't want something so boring.

03:47.018 --> 03:47.852
Uran!

03:47.936 --> 03:50.355
I'd rather be awarded that lion.

03:50.438 --> 03:52.649
Please excuse her.
We'll be on our way now.

03:55.318 --> 03:56.444
Inspector!

03:57.028 --> 04:00.448
He's here, at the entrance.

04:00.531 --> 04:02.784
What? Where's Superintendent Tawashi?

04:02.867 --> 04:03.993
I've contacted him.

04:04.077 --> 04:04.994
Good!

04:06.579 --> 04:09.958
Uran, how many times must I tell you?
Don't take detours.

04:10.041 --> 04:12.293
But I couldn't help it.

04:13.503 --> 04:14.921
Hey, wait.

04:15.505 --> 04:16.923
You two are this way.

04:21.886 --> 04:24.013
No, we're supposed to go this way.

04:24.097 --> 04:26.391
Huh? Really?

04:28.559 --> 04:31.187
It's hard to tell these days...

04:31.271 --> 04:33.690
Right this way, please.

04:53.835 --> 04:55.670
Are you listening to me, Atom?

04:55.753 --> 04:56.921
Huh? Yeah.

04:57.797 --> 05:03.344
Like I said, I wasn't taking a detour,
and you wouldn't believe what I saw.

05:07.348 --> 05:11.185
Thank you so much for coming.

05:11.269 --> 05:14.480
I am Tawashi of
the Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department.

05:21.154 --> 05:24.532
- Hey, get me a translation machine!
- Yes, right away!

05:25.116 --> 05:27.994
No need. I can speak Japanese.

05:28.077 --> 05:33.541
I see. Just what you'd expect from
Central Asia's greatest intellect, huh?

05:33.624 --> 05:34.959
Yes, indeed!

05:37.420 --> 05:38.755
Please have a seat.

05:38.838 --> 05:42.925
I apologize for the drab surroundings,
Professor Abullah.

05:43.009 --> 05:45.636
Not at all.
Everywhere in Japan is fantastic,

05:45.720 --> 05:49.307
especially compared to the current state
of my home country, Persia.

05:51.059 --> 05:54.354
Is this visit part
of the post-war reconstruction efforts?

05:54.937 --> 05:55.980
That's right.

05:56.064 --> 05:59.192
I'm here to attend
the World Science Conference in Tokyo.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.029
By the way, Professor Abullah,

06:03.696 --> 06:06.741
you also visited Japan
three months ago, correct?

06:07.367 --> 06:08.201
I did.

06:08.284 --> 06:12.705
And you met a legal scholar
named Junichiro Tazaki, didn't you?

06:16.125 --> 06:18.419
I heard the shocking news.

06:19.045 --> 06:23.466
<i>Why did a great man like him
have to be killed?</i>

06:24.467 --> 06:27.637
You were the last person
to see Mr. Tazaki alive.

06:29.680 --> 06:33.059
Please rest assured.
You're not under suspicion.

06:33.643 --> 06:37.772
The incident happened as your plane
was about to depart from the airport.

06:38.731 --> 06:42.819
It's just that we wondered if you noticed
anything out of the ordinary.

06:45.405 --> 06:48.699
He had so many wonderful things
to tell me.

06:49.575 --> 06:52.662
Mr. Tazaki was the first to propose
the International Robot Laws.

06:53.413 --> 06:56.124
It was his true and sincere wish

06:56.833 --> 06:59.585
for robots and humans to coexist.

07:03.631 --> 07:08.052
Robots actually feel a lot more
than humans assume, don't you think?

07:09.011 --> 07:10.012
Yeah.

07:10.096 --> 07:14.392
But we're just not good
at expressing ourselves.

07:15.059 --> 07:18.688
They say they can't tell
humans from robots without a sensor gate,

07:18.771 --> 07:19.939
but I can tell right away.

07:20.606 --> 07:23.025
Humans have
complicated facial expressions.

07:23.901 --> 07:25.403
Like this.

07:27.238 --> 07:28.364
That man...

07:29.115 --> 07:30.324
Which man?

07:30.908 --> 07:33.119
The man we passed by at the gate.

07:33.703 --> 07:34.704
I couldn't tell

07:35.955 --> 07:37.582
<i>if he was human or robot.</i>

07:39.917 --> 07:42.587
Thank you for your cooperation.

07:42.670 --> 07:45.131
Not at all. I'm sorry I wasn't much help.

07:50.428 --> 07:52.930
Hey! I told you to turn it off!

07:53.014 --> 07:54.682
- I'm sorry!
- The professor--

07:54.765 --> 07:59.145
I lost most of my organic body
in the last war.

08:00.938 --> 08:02.607
I beg your pardon!

08:03.191 --> 08:05.401
Oh, please don't worry.

08:08.654 --> 08:13.034
By the way, I heard today
there was another tornado in Tokyo.

08:13.117 --> 08:14.494
Yes.

08:15.912 --> 08:17.455
Where did it happen?

08:20.791 --> 08:21.876
Fear...

08:23.294 --> 08:25.546
But the big cats are okay now, right?

08:30.384 --> 08:33.429
The feeling I had today
came flying at superspeed.

08:34.305 --> 08:36.140
Like, whoosh!

08:36.807 --> 08:39.101
You mean apart from the big cats?

08:39.936 --> 08:41.562
I'm not sure.

08:41.646 --> 08:44.774
And you're still getting that feeling?

08:46.984 --> 08:48.486
It's really faint.

08:49.070 --> 08:50.196
From which way?

08:50.905 --> 08:52.698
It's too faint to tell.

08:55.743 --> 09:00.081
You know, lions hide their fear
when they're really scared.

09:03.376 --> 09:04.377
But right now,

09:05.378 --> 09:07.255
the one who's most scared

09:08.256 --> 09:09.215
is you, Atom!

09:57.805 --> 09:59.265
You were looking at it again.

10:02.518 --> 10:04.395
Don't blame yourself so much.

10:06.856 --> 10:08.399
- Hey, Helena.
- Yes?

10:08.983 --> 10:10.026
Let's take a trip.

10:11.152 --> 10:11.986
A trip?

10:12.695 --> 10:14.196
We discussed it the other day.

10:14.697 --> 10:17.033
But can you take time off?

10:17.116 --> 10:20.953
The higher-ups consider the robot attacks
to be concluded for now.

10:21.662 --> 10:24.165
True. And a change of pace might be good.

10:24.874 --> 10:25.708
It will be.

10:26.208 --> 10:27.126
I'm sure of it.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.337
How about Japan?

10:29.837 --> 10:30.838
Japan?

10:31.672 --> 10:34.884
I was just there for work,
and it was a lovely place.

10:35.551 --> 10:36.677
I'll leave it to you.

10:41.390 --> 10:42.975
<i>This is Marco Polo Tourist.</i>

10:43.059 --> 10:45.519
Hello, I used your service before.

10:46.062 --> 10:47.355
<i>Mr. Gesicht, yes?</i>

10:47.855 --> 10:49.857
I'd like to make a reservation again.

10:49.940 --> 10:50.983
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

10:51.692 --> 10:53.736
My wife and I would like to go to Japan.

10:53.819 --> 10:54.945
<i>Very well.</i>

10:55.780 --> 10:59.659
I guess I'll have to register her
with you first.

10:59.742 --> 11:02.953
<i>Actually, your wife is already registered.</i>

11:06.874 --> 11:10.294
I don't believe she's left
the Euro Federation before.

11:10.961 --> 11:13.923
<i>Both of you have registered
with us before,</i>

11:14.006 --> 11:15.758
<i>but you canceled your reservation.</i>

11:16.425 --> 11:18.219
- We did?
<i>-</i> When?

11:19.095 --> 11:23.182
<i>Two years ago. It was the same request
for a trip to Japan.</i>

11:24.141 --> 11:26.519
Two years ago to Japan?

11:30.398 --> 11:34.110
<i>Two years ago, we were in Spain</i>

11:34.193 --> 11:37.071
for my training assignment with Europol.

11:37.154 --> 11:38.322
That's right.

11:38.948 --> 11:41.033
We lived in Madrid for the entire year.

11:41.617 --> 11:43.244
See? We have tons of photos.

11:47.790 --> 11:50.251
Ah, this is the Sagrada Família.

11:51.252 --> 11:52.920
This is Andalusia.

11:53.713 --> 11:58.676
You tripped and disappeared
into the field of sunflowers.

11:58.759 --> 12:03.597
I remember!
You even used your GPS to find me.

12:07.685 --> 12:10.062
We sure took a lot of pictures.

12:10.604 --> 12:11.480
Yes.

12:20.781 --> 12:21.907
Maybe too many?

12:22.491 --> 12:26.912
Right. We do try to copy human behavior,
but we never take this many photos.

12:28.497 --> 12:29.790
It was fun, wasn't it?

12:30.374 --> 12:32.126
Yes. Very.

12:33.169 --> 12:36.338
Apparently, we planned
a trip to Japan during that time.

12:52.313 --> 12:54.398
<i>All done, Gesicht.</i>

12:55.024 --> 12:56.984
<i>No abnormalities at all.</i>

12:57.526 --> 12:58.903
Thank you, Professor Hoffman.

13:02.656 --> 13:05.159
<i>Since you insisted on coming in,</i>

13:05.242 --> 13:08.037
<i>I don't doubt you're experiencing
some sort of malfunction.</i>

13:08.120 --> 13:11.582
But according to the data,
everything looks just fine.

13:11.665 --> 13:14.168
I still think it's due to fatigue.

13:17.129 --> 13:20.299
And don't be too hard on yourself
about what happened to Brando.

13:23.010 --> 13:26.806
Human memory is a convenient thing.

13:27.431 --> 13:29.683
We have the function to forget.

13:30.601 --> 13:34.814
Life can be tough if you hang on
to too many painful memories.

13:35.940 --> 13:38.275
That's what forgetting is for.

13:39.944 --> 13:42.530
But it doesn't work that way with robots.

13:43.322 --> 13:45.616
Your memory will always remain fresh.

13:46.617 --> 13:48.702
The only solution for robot memories

13:48.786 --> 13:49.995
is to delete them.

13:51.789 --> 13:52.665
Professor.

13:52.748 --> 13:53.582
Yes?

13:54.124 --> 13:57.169
Is there any record
of my memories being deleted?

14:00.840 --> 14:03.175
No, I don't see any record of that.

14:03.926 --> 14:07.054
How about traces
of nonfactual memories being inserted?

14:07.680 --> 14:10.182
You mean like false memories?

14:10.683 --> 14:11.517
Yes.

14:12.268 --> 14:16.272
I heard things like that used to be done
at correctional facilities,

14:16.355 --> 14:19.024
but now robots have rights too.

14:19.650 --> 14:21.485
Why do you ask?

14:22.278 --> 14:27.032
What if someone had deleted my memories
and replaced them with false memories?

14:28.784 --> 14:31.328
What if that's the reason
for my nightmares?

14:35.291 --> 14:37.501
That's an interesting theory.

14:45.759 --> 14:48.596
I'm off to a meeting now.
Can we talk later?

14:48.679 --> 14:51.557
I only need a minute, Director Schelling!

14:52.141 --> 14:53.684
We'll talk later.

14:53.767 --> 14:56.437
Did you do something
to Detective Gesicht's memory?

15:05.404 --> 15:06.906
Director!

15:09.909 --> 15:13.329
How many robots of Gesicht's caliber
are left in the world?

15:13.829 --> 15:14.788
What?

15:15.789 --> 15:18.417
How many robots have existed in the world

15:18.918 --> 15:21.170
that could become
weapons of mass destruction?

15:21.921 --> 15:24.131
There were seven altogether.

15:24.715 --> 15:25.633
That's right.

15:25.716 --> 15:28.218
And now, in this series of incidents,

15:28.302 --> 15:32.097
three of them, Mont Blanc, North No.2,
and Brando, have been destroyed.

15:32.681 --> 15:35.684
Now, there are only four left.

15:35.768 --> 15:37.561
And one of them

15:38.771 --> 15:40.022
is Gesicht.

15:41.523 --> 15:43.567
But, Director,
that doesn’t answer my question!

15:43.651 --> 15:46.570
Did you do something to him?
His artificial intelligence--

15:46.654 --> 15:49.698
We made a huge investment
in Gesicht, you know!

15:52.451 --> 15:55.621
All you need to do
is to maintain him properly.

15:57.289 --> 15:58.624
That's all.

16:01.335 --> 16:03.045
What did you do to Gesicht?

16:05.839 --> 16:08.634
What exactly are you hiding?

16:15.265 --> 16:16.934
These horns...

16:18.060 --> 16:21.188
You think it's the same killer
from the other cases?

16:22.398 --> 16:24.566
What do you make of this,
Detective Gesicht?

16:25.442 --> 16:27.611
No, this is a copycat.

16:28.195 --> 16:29.071
How do you know?

16:29.738 --> 16:33.534
The perpetrator wore hybrid sneakers
to try and conceal their footprints,

16:34.368 --> 16:36.870
but I see traces of movements everywhere.

16:38.789 --> 16:40.416
Weight: 78 kilograms.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.501
Height: 175 centimeters.

16:43.085 --> 16:44.461
Most importantly, that drawer.

16:45.379 --> 16:49.800
The culprit had difficulty with the knob,
so they removed their gloves for a moment.

16:50.592 --> 16:52.428
You'll find fingerprints on it.

16:53.012 --> 16:53.887
Forensics!

16:54.430 --> 16:57.391
So this is a robbery
made to look like those incidents?

16:58.017 --> 16:59.601
Yes, most likely.

16:59.685 --> 17:02.980
Amazing as ever. You're perfect.

17:05.524 --> 17:06.442
Perfect.

17:07.067 --> 17:08.944
You're on vacation, right?

17:09.028 --> 17:12.156
I'm sorry for summoning you.
You've been a great help.

17:15.242 --> 17:17.119
- Detective Fersen.
- Yes?

17:18.370 --> 17:21.081
This is the second time
we've met, correct?

17:22.624 --> 17:26.045
Come on, I'm sure your robot memory
is more accurate than mine!

17:26.670 --> 17:30.507
We met in Salzburg three years ago.
You did an excellent job on that case too.

17:31.592 --> 17:32.468
Three years ago?

17:32.551 --> 17:38.182
Yes, right after you came back
from The 39th Central Asian War.

17:38.766 --> 17:41.435
I remember you telling me
all those stories from the war.

17:42.102 --> 17:46.190
You had seven beers
at Karl's bar that night.

17:47.441 --> 17:49.985
So you do remember!

17:50.069 --> 17:51.653
And I'm still a beer drinker.

17:52.529 --> 17:54.615
It was great to see you again, Detective.

17:55.657 --> 17:56.575
Same here.

17:57.201 --> 17:59.161
Let's go for drinks again another time.

18:02.664 --> 18:05.793
<i>I remember perfectly
what happened three years ago.</i>

18:06.376 --> 18:10.089
<i>It's been four years since the end
of The 39th Central Asian War.</i>

18:10.172 --> 18:12.591
<i>Democracy is starting
to take root in Persia...</i>

18:12.674 --> 18:16.011
<i>The 39th Central Asian War...</i>

18:22.434 --> 18:24.645
<i>We're military police!</i>

18:25.687 --> 18:28.649
<i>There are terrorists hiding in this area!</i>

18:29.399 --> 18:32.903
<i>All residents must evacuate immediately!</i>

18:33.612 --> 18:34.863
<i>I repeat!</i>

18:34.947 --> 18:36.615
<i>There are terrorists hiding...</i>

18:51.797 --> 18:52.881
They're not here.

18:54.925 --> 18:57.594
There aren't any terrorists here!

18:59.638 --> 19:03.016
The only ones here were children!

19:03.100 --> 19:07.437
You dropped a bomb on my sleeping child!

19:10.274 --> 19:13.569
To hell with "saving the oppressed"!

19:13.652 --> 19:16.572
Is killing children your idea of justice?

19:16.655 --> 19:18.532
Have you no humanity?

19:18.615 --> 19:21.493
You must know how I feel!

19:21.994 --> 19:23.370
I am a robot.

19:27.916 --> 19:28.792
Stop it!

19:43.056 --> 19:43.891
He's...

19:44.433 --> 19:45.559
He's in despair.

19:46.059 --> 19:49.438
It may be an emotion beyond understanding
for a robot like you.

19:54.151 --> 19:55.360
Despair...

19:59.239 --> 20:02.034
<i>My memory from four years ago
is perfect too.</i>

20:17.007 --> 20:18.425
I got killed!

20:20.469 --> 20:22.554
- Aw, man!
- Oh no, I'm sorry.

20:22.638 --> 20:25.641
- I just got this yesterday, Mom!
- Hans.

20:25.724 --> 20:28.477
Why can't we get a maid robot?

20:28.560 --> 20:30.145
My whole class has one, but--

20:30.229 --> 20:31.480
Hans!

20:31.563 --> 20:34.483
Your mother is doing the best she can.

20:34.983 --> 20:36.443
Watch your words.

20:37.027 --> 20:39.404
Besides, no gaming during meals.

20:40.197 --> 20:41.156
Yes, sir.

20:47.079 --> 20:48.872
What's your plan for today, dear?

20:50.624 --> 20:52.918
Today's the anniversary
of your brother's death.

20:55.087 --> 20:57.256
You're going to go claim his body,
aren't you?

20:59.925 --> 21:02.511
Yes, today makes three years.

21:03.136 --> 21:07.140
I still can't believe they wouldn't
let you have it for three whole years.

21:07.766 --> 21:09.935
It's the law.

21:10.018 --> 21:13.105
The authorities keep
the bodies of criminals for three years.

21:13.772 --> 21:16.608
It can't be helped.
He was a rotten apple, after all.

21:21.113 --> 21:22.030
But you know,

21:22.990 --> 21:25.993
he was a good brother to me.

21:26.618 --> 21:28.787
I want to give him a proper burial,

21:29.496 --> 21:30.872
regardless of who he was.

21:34.876 --> 21:38.213
<i>An explosion occurred
at a hotel in Berlin last night.</i>

21:38.839 --> 21:42.217
<i>Judge Neuman from the German Ministry
of Justice has been confirmed dead.</i>

21:42.843 --> 21:46.972
<i>Judge Neuman attracted attention
as the world's first robot judge</i>

21:47.055 --> 21:52.227
<i>and was known for groundbreaking verdicts
on cases such as the Greifelt lawsuit.</i>

21:52.936 --> 21:57.065
<i>The cause of the explosion is under
investigation, and according to forensi--</i>

22:00.402 --> 22:02.529
<i>Good morning, Adolf.</i>

22:03.238 --> 22:04.990
I heard the news.

22:06.158 --> 22:07.451
<i>What news?</i>

22:08.243 --> 22:12.414
A robot judge was killed... No, destroyed.

22:14.416 --> 22:15.876
<i>Death to machines.</i>

22:18.587 --> 22:19.838
Death to machines.

22:20.422 --> 22:21.965
<i>Death to machines.</i>

22:22.758 --> 22:24.301
Death to machines!

22:33.852 --> 22:36.897
Corpse number 902886.

22:38.065 --> 22:39.024
Right this way.

22:40.484 --> 22:42.861
In accordance with the König Law,

22:42.944 --> 22:44.821
we acknowledge the passage of three years

22:44.905 --> 22:47.616
and hereby return the body
to the family of the deceased.

22:48.116 --> 22:49.743
Will you accept it?

22:49.826 --> 22:50.744
Yes.

22:51.661 --> 22:53.330
Then please sign here.

22:55.582 --> 22:59.294
I don't need to look
at my brother's body, do I?

22:59.378 --> 23:02.756
Given the degree of his injuries,
I would not recommend it.

23:04.049 --> 23:06.718
I was told he was shot to death
by a police officer.

23:07.469 --> 23:09.679
And it was lawful and appropriate.

23:16.686 --> 23:18.563
<i>Please state your destination.</i>

23:19.648 --> 23:21.483
Hofgarten Cemetery.

23:21.566 --> 23:22.651
<i>Confirmed.</i>

23:28.115 --> 23:30.617
Scratch that. New destination.

23:31.410 --> 23:32.536
To Dr. Schiller's.

23:33.578 --> 23:34.621
<i>Confirmed.</i>

23:36.832 --> 23:39.709
I'm sorry to drop by unannounced, Doctor.

23:39.793 --> 23:43.380
So, you want me
to view your brother's body?

23:43.463 --> 23:44.297
Yes.

23:46.466 --> 23:48.969
You have a problem
with the autopsy report?

23:49.052 --> 23:50.595
No, not exactly.

23:51.096 --> 23:53.223
Well, it's a chance to say goodbye.

23:53.723 --> 23:54.891
Let's see.

23:56.601 --> 23:57.769
This is...

23:57.853 --> 23:58.854
Doctor?

24:13.410 --> 24:14.494
What's the matter?

24:15.078 --> 24:17.706
No, it's nothing.

24:29.843 --> 24:33.680
We see more and more robots these days,
even in places like this.

24:39.019 --> 24:42.189
They say robots can think like we do,

24:42.814 --> 24:44.024
but who knows--

24:45.442 --> 24:48.945
Don't say things like that too loud.

24:49.029 --> 24:50.530
It'd be discrimination.

24:50.614 --> 24:53.366
At least under
Universal Robot Rights Protection Laws.

24:55.577 --> 24:58.788
I have one other thing
to take care of before I go home.

24:58.872 --> 25:00.582
You go on ahead without me.

25:00.665 --> 25:02.459
Okay. Be careful.

25:03.168 --> 25:05.795
<i>Armed robbery in progress!
There are multiple suspects!</i>

25:05.879 --> 25:07.923
<i>They're fleeing
in a military-armed vehicle!</i>

25:08.006 --> 25:10.383
<i>The suspects broke through Ward N-6!</i>

25:10.467 --> 25:12.594
This is Gesicht.
I'll try and head them off.

25:25.941 --> 25:30.320
I have eyes on the suspects' vehicle.
Requesting permission to fire the SAAW!

25:30.403 --> 25:31.530
<i>Permitted!</i>

25:34.866 --> 25:36.660
Did you get them, Gesicht?

25:36.743 --> 25:39.246
I only damaged the tires of the vehicle.

25:42.207 --> 25:44.042
Hands in the air!

25:44.125 --> 25:45.335
Freeze, or we'll shoot!

25:48.213 --> 25:49.714
Splendid, Gesicht.

25:50.549 --> 25:52.592
Is that a specialized anti-tank gun?

25:52.676 --> 25:57.264
No, I had to use a special shell
to stop an armored vehicle like that.

25:58.223 --> 25:59.975
What is it, then?

26:00.850 --> 26:01.935
A special alloy.

26:02.561 --> 26:03.895
Zeronium shells.

26:13.989 --> 26:15.073
Brethren!

26:15.156 --> 26:21.246
My wish is to eradicate every single robot
from the face of this planet.

26:21.830 --> 26:25.750
Now is the time
to teach those abhorrent machines!

26:26.293 --> 26:29.087
I will promise you all this.

26:29.170 --> 26:31.673
Repeal the Universal Robot Rights
Protection Laws!

26:31.756 --> 26:34.884
Repeal the Universal Robot Rights
Protection Laws!

26:34.968 --> 26:37.095
Abolish police-bots!

26:37.178 --> 26:39.306
Abolish police-bots!

26:39.389 --> 26:41.766
Robots are servants!

26:41.850 --> 26:44.227
Robots are servants!

26:44.311 --> 26:46.271
Robots are slaves!

26:46.354 --> 26:48.315
Robots are slaves!

26:48.398 --> 26:50.233
Robots are inferior.

26:50.317 --> 26:52.193
Robots are inferior!

26:52.277 --> 26:54.404
Death to machines.

26:54.487 --> 26:58.199
Death to machines!

26:58.283 --> 27:01.786
Death to machines!

27:11.171 --> 27:13.298
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

27:16.009 --> 27:16.968
So...

27:19.179 --> 27:21.348
What is this urgent matter you spoke of?

27:22.349 --> 27:24.809
I claimed my brother's body today.

27:25.393 --> 27:26.519
I see...

27:26.603 --> 27:27.520
<i>That</i> brother.

27:28.521 --> 27:32.442
He was the kind of person
who deserved to be killed.

27:32.525 --> 27:34.319
- But...
- But?

27:34.819 --> 27:35.987
He was pulverized.

27:36.738 --> 27:38.198
"Pulverized"?

27:38.907 --> 27:42.160
They used a weapon
that should never be used against humans.

27:42.827 --> 27:45.997
I was told the only ones capable
of firing a weapon of that caliber

27:46.748 --> 27:48.458
are robots and no others.

27:48.541 --> 27:52.837
What? If that's true,
it would be a huge scandal.

27:52.921 --> 27:56.216
Yes, Article 13
of the International Robot Laws says,

27:56.716 --> 27:59.803
"A robot shall not be able
to hurt or kill humans."

28:00.679 --> 28:05.475
There are only a few robots in the world
that can fire such an armament.

28:06.059 --> 28:08.019
And that armament is?

28:08.603 --> 28:10.980
It's a special Zeronium alloy shell.

28:11.564 --> 28:13.024
I see.

28:13.108 --> 28:15.443
I know the robot you speak of.

28:17.404 --> 28:18.947
Detective Gesicht.

28:19.030 --> 28:23.660
A robot in whose development Europol
made their largest-ever investment.

28:24.327 --> 28:27.622
He has solved many difficult cases.

28:27.706 --> 28:31.126
During The 39th Central Asian War,

28:31.209 --> 28:33.837
he served as a member
of the peacekeeping forces.

28:33.920 --> 28:39.259
If he murdered your brother,

28:39.342 --> 28:41.428
it's repulsive to even imagine it.

28:43.555 --> 28:44.514
My brother,

28:45.098 --> 28:46.850
he was a lowlife.

28:47.892 --> 28:49.519
But still,

28:50.228 --> 28:53.398
he didn't deserve
to be pulverized by a robot!

28:55.233 --> 28:57.944
I couldn't agree more, Adolf.

28:58.528 --> 28:59.821
Lend me your strength!

29:00.613 --> 29:03.116
The strength to destroy this robot!

29:10.623 --> 29:11.833
It's been a while.

29:12.584 --> 29:16.045
I haven't worn this battle suit
since the war.

29:18.590 --> 29:19.674
You kept it maintained?

29:19.758 --> 29:24.429
I did what I could.
I had to be discreet, you see?

29:24.512 --> 29:26.681
But taking a battle suit
without permission...

29:27.265 --> 29:29.642
I owe you. I know I've asked a lot of you.

29:30.226 --> 29:32.687
Well, we go back a long way.

29:32.771 --> 29:35.648
But what are you going to do?

29:35.732 --> 29:37.901
If they find out,
they'll revoke your license!

29:38.985 --> 29:40.153
I don't mind.

29:40.236 --> 29:41.112
What?

29:42.655 --> 29:43.948
I'm retiring.

29:49.746 --> 29:50.705
Hercules.

29:50.789 --> 29:53.291
There's nothing
like a military battle suit!

29:53.374 --> 29:56.044
The horsepower is way different
than in my pankration suit.

29:56.127 --> 29:57.253
Yeah.

29:59.422 --> 30:01.883
The left arm output feels a bit weak.

30:02.759 --> 30:04.803
Okay, I'll work on it.

30:09.015 --> 30:10.308
Two suns?

30:11.893 --> 30:12.769
Hercules!

30:16.189 --> 30:20.527
A police robot used a Zeronium shell
just the other day.

30:21.110 --> 30:24.405
Care to comment, Spokesperson Wagner
of the Europol Information Office?

30:24.489 --> 30:27.575
Yes, it was against an armored vehicle.

30:27.659 --> 30:30.703
But if it happens to hit a human,
they'll be pulverized.

30:31.287 --> 30:34.332
Any use of it requires permission
from headquarters,

30:34.415 --> 30:36.584
and we make sure
that human lives are protected.

30:37.168 --> 30:38.753
But there can always be mistakes!

30:38.837 --> 30:41.047
Well, we make sure
human lives are absolutely--

30:41.130 --> 30:45.051
Exactly how many robots
are capable of firing Zeronium shells?

30:47.804 --> 30:52.725
<i>It's like we humans walk the streets
under constant watch of an executioner.</i>

30:53.268 --> 30:56.187
<i>The discussion is heating up,
but let's take a commercial break.</i>

30:56.271 --> 30:57.397
What do you think?

30:57.981 --> 31:00.400
It's a TV program we've set up.

31:00.483 --> 31:03.361
Our media strategy
is steadily making progress.

31:03.444 --> 31:05.572
But it will take time.

31:06.155 --> 31:08.032
There's no need to rush

31:08.116 --> 31:11.536
as long as
we can stigmatize Gesicht in the end.

31:11.619 --> 31:14.289
I've looked into his schedule.

31:14.789 --> 31:17.876
He's going on a long vacation
in a few days' time.

31:17.959 --> 31:19.252
We have to act now!

31:19.335 --> 31:24.716
Please. No matter where he runs,
we will never stop denouncing him.

31:24.799 --> 31:25.967
But...

31:26.050 --> 31:29.470
If we rush, your brother's background
will come out as well.

31:30.179 --> 31:35.935
To be honest, even I feel nauseous
hearing about the things he did.

31:38.479 --> 31:40.523
If those facts are publicly revealed,

31:40.607 --> 31:44.110
then society will turn against us, and you
can forget the anti-robot campaign.

31:45.361 --> 31:46.905
You understand, don't you?

31:49.657 --> 31:52.285
Hold on. Where are you going?

32:04.505 --> 32:05.798
Hercules!

32:09.427 --> 32:10.261
Are you okay?

32:10.345 --> 32:12.388
This energy reaction...

32:12.931 --> 32:14.474
Is it Photon Energy?

32:18.311 --> 32:19.479
Epsilon!

32:28.696 --> 32:31.449
That was a rough way to say hello
for our first meeting.

32:32.450 --> 32:33.785
I apologize.

32:34.369 --> 32:37.163
But I felt I needed to stop you.

32:37.872 --> 32:38.706
Stop me?

32:39.207 --> 32:41.042
It's still alive, isn't it?

32:41.125 --> 32:45.672
The enemy that destroyed
Mont Blanc, North No.2, and Brando.

32:45.755 --> 32:47.674
Don't forget you're a target too.

32:48.675 --> 32:49.634
I know.

32:50.343 --> 32:51.511
Then why stop me?

32:52.011 --> 32:53.554
We must not fight.

32:55.139 --> 32:56.349
A pacifist, are you?

32:56.975 --> 33:00.019
Is that why you refused
to be deployed to that war?

33:00.979 --> 33:03.022
That war did not have a righteous cause.

33:03.606 --> 33:04.732
"A righteous cause"?

33:05.358 --> 33:08.236
Even though so many robots were destroyed?

33:09.988 --> 33:11.990
You're just scared.

33:12.532 --> 33:14.575
And you're justifying it with excuses.

33:15.243 --> 33:17.203
Yes, I am scared.

33:19.539 --> 33:22.208
I heard you were forced
to do post-war cleanup

33:22.291 --> 33:24.460
under terrible conditions because of that.

33:25.503 --> 33:27.922
I was abused and heckled
by the entire world,

33:28.423 --> 33:30.466
unlike you heroes.

33:32.051 --> 33:35.138
But thanks to that,
I gained something valuable.

33:35.221 --> 33:36.389
Something valuable?

33:37.765 --> 33:39.976
<i>I met many war orphans.</i>

33:40.476 --> 33:43.688
<i>I took them in, and I'm raising them.</i>

33:44.647 --> 33:48.026
Yeah, I heard.
A robot raising human children.

33:48.609 --> 33:50.695
Yet another reason to criticize you.

33:51.571 --> 33:55.658
This valuable thing you mentioned.
Could it be love?

33:58.202 --> 34:02.331
I'm sure you gained something
from the war, didn't you?

34:05.501 --> 34:07.545
The ability to hate, perhaps?

34:09.380 --> 34:10.631
Here is what I think.

34:11.132 --> 34:13.342
Humans and robots are growing closer.

34:14.385 --> 34:15.887
And if we get too close,

34:16.679 --> 34:18.222
something bad will happen.

34:20.475 --> 34:22.018
Here is what I think.

34:22.810 --> 34:24.437
This is the first sign.

34:25.563 --> 34:26.898
A sign?

34:27.815 --> 34:29.358
We must break...

34:32.445 --> 34:33.863
this cycle of hate.

34:37.366 --> 34:40.244
This isn't an item
you can just find anywhere, pal.

34:40.328 --> 34:45.500
It was used in the Central Asian War,
but you can't make or sell them anymore.

34:46.125 --> 34:49.962
It's a compact cluster cannon.
A guided rocket launcher.

34:50.546 --> 34:54.717
It locks onto its target and never misses.

34:54.801 --> 34:57.929
It'll explode inside the body.
Even a robot will be blown to bits.

34:58.596 --> 35:01.015
Whoa there. Be careful with that thing.

35:01.099 --> 35:04.268
Possession is enough for civilians
to be charged with attempted murder.

35:06.062 --> 35:07.146
I won't kill.

35:07.897 --> 35:09.065
Not humans, at least.

35:15.571 --> 35:16.823
<i>When I was a child,</i>

35:16.906 --> 35:21.869
<i>the use of robots
dramatically improved productivity.</i>

35:21.953 --> 35:23.287
<i>At the same time,</i>

35:23.371 --> 35:25.123
<i>because of the so-called
"robot restructure,"</i>

35:25.206 --> 35:27.333
<i>many unemployed humans
ended up on the streets.</i>

35:27.917 --> 35:30.128
<i>My father was one of the victims.</i>

35:30.628 --> 35:33.297
Dad, I'm hungry!

35:35.591 --> 35:37.677
Let's grab something to eat.

35:39.387 --> 35:42.098
Man, just another sandwich.

35:42.974 --> 35:44.809
I want to eat some steak.

35:44.892 --> 35:47.270
Get real, you idiot!

35:47.895 --> 35:50.565
You think Dad found a decent job?

35:51.065 --> 35:53.860
He's looking because he hasn't found one.

35:54.819 --> 35:56.028
It'll be all right.

35:56.112 --> 35:57.321
Don't you worry.

35:57.405 --> 36:00.283
Dad, when is Mom coming back?

36:03.035 --> 36:04.245
It's all right.

36:04.328 --> 36:05.496
Don't you worry.

36:08.708 --> 36:10.251
I wish we had a ball.

36:16.799 --> 36:18.134
Here you go. It's a ball.

36:18.843 --> 36:22.180
Huh? Wow, it's brand-new!

36:22.263 --> 36:23.514
Where did you get it?

36:24.182 --> 36:26.475
Don't worry about it. Go play.

36:27.185 --> 36:28.519
Thank you, Dad!

36:32.773 --> 36:33.608
There!

36:34.817 --> 36:35.693
There!

36:35.776 --> 36:36.694
Hey!

36:40.907 --> 36:42.366
He is the culprit.

36:42.450 --> 36:45.578
He stole the ball from the store.

36:45.661 --> 36:48.122
It wasn't me! I didn't do it!

36:48.206 --> 36:50.583
He is the culprit.

36:51.292 --> 36:53.544
I'm sorry, okay? Please let me go!

36:55.171 --> 36:56.005
Damn it!

36:56.797 --> 36:58.049
Forgive me!

36:58.132 --> 36:59.300
Ah, damn it!

37:00.301 --> 37:02.511
<i>He came home a couple days later</i>

37:03.262 --> 37:05.431
<i>and started to drink heavily.</i>

37:06.724 --> 37:07.850
<i>Three months later,</i>

37:09.143 --> 37:11.020
<i>he jumped from the roof of our building.</i>

37:15.983 --> 37:16.943
What's wrong?

37:18.152 --> 37:21.280
Adolf, you wanted this, right?

37:22.990 --> 37:23.866
Here you go.

37:25.701 --> 37:28.454
Hey, this is a portable prep school!

37:29.622 --> 37:30.831
What happened to your arm?

37:33.084 --> 37:34.669
I had to off them.

37:35.169 --> 37:36.420
"Off them"?

37:36.504 --> 37:38.130
A robot.

37:38.214 --> 37:40.716
They can't kill us humans,

37:41.300 --> 37:44.637
but we're allowed to kill them.

37:48.307 --> 37:49.934
Study hard, Adolf.

37:50.559 --> 37:53.896
Study hard
and create a world without robots.

38:11.789 --> 38:13.040
Toward the suburbs?

38:13.791 --> 38:15.543
Did he notice me tailing him?

38:31.642 --> 38:32.893
Maybe this is my chance.

38:39.150 --> 38:40.276
<i>What is he up to?</i>

38:43.696 --> 38:44.572
This is it!

38:47.074 --> 38:48.034
Damn it!

38:58.294 --> 38:59.795
You're Epsilon, I presume?

39:00.421 --> 39:03.215
I'm sorry to have asked you
to come on such short notice.

39:03.299 --> 39:07.053
It's fine. It's not something to discuss
over a simple data transfer.

39:07.636 --> 39:11.265
You are the only one
with the authority to arrest our enemy.

39:11.932 --> 39:14.518
The enemy died fighting Brando.

39:15.144 --> 39:17.813
That's the official line
from Europol as well.

39:17.897 --> 39:20.399
Do you really believe that?

39:21.984 --> 39:23.694
We must stop Hercules.

39:24.278 --> 39:27.865
We must prevent a duel,
a worst-case scenario.

39:29.367 --> 39:30.409
That goes for you too.

39:31.077 --> 39:32.745
No need to tell me that.

39:32.828 --> 39:34.121
I am a police officer.

39:34.705 --> 39:36.749
We must act, or another war will start.

39:38.042 --> 39:40.461
War must never occur again.

39:42.880 --> 39:48.135
No one should experience what the children
in my care went through.

39:50.721 --> 39:55.559
Have you heard of what they're calling
Persian War Syndrome?

39:56.143 --> 39:57.144
Yes.

39:57.228 --> 40:01.148
Deep psychological damage
from the experiences of the war.

40:01.649 --> 40:05.152
Many of the children in my care
suffer from severe symptoms.

40:05.820 --> 40:07.279
Especially one in particular.

40:08.572 --> 40:11.575
His entire village
disappeared in an instant.

40:12.618 --> 40:14.453
He was the sole survivor.

40:14.537 --> 40:16.455
<i>Everything and everyone was simply gone.</i>

40:19.166 --> 40:21.460
<i>An image is burned into his memory.</i>

40:23.838 --> 40:26.549
<i>Something huge moving toward the desert.</i>

40:29.885 --> 40:32.346
Even today, he only speaks one word.

40:35.391 --> 40:39.270
It's the word uttered
by the thing he saw that day.

40:41.605 --> 40:42.731
Bora.

40:58.539 --> 40:59.415
Atom!

41:00.416 --> 41:03.002
What's wrong?
We gotta hurry, or we'll be late.

41:03.085 --> 41:06.422
Hey, Atom, did you feel anything?

41:06.505 --> 41:07.465
Feel what?

41:08.007 --> 41:13.512
Like a small animal quivering in fear
because it can't find its way home?

41:13.596 --> 41:14.597
Again?

41:14.680 --> 41:16.182
I'm going to go find it!

41:16.974 --> 41:18.100
What about school?

41:18.184 --> 41:19.643
Think of an excuse for me!

41:21.562 --> 41:23.314
She's nothing but trouble.

41:26.358 --> 41:28.235
REDEVELOPMENT ZONE
NO TRESPASSING

41:31.113 --> 41:32.198
Is it this way?

41:34.366 --> 41:35.701
What on earth is this?

41:36.243 --> 41:38.078
Such a terrible painting.

41:49.673 --> 41:50.508
Hey.

41:51.008 --> 41:52.009
Are you dead?

41:54.637 --> 41:56.430
Were you the one crying?

41:58.307 --> 42:00.392
You're a robot, aren't you?

42:01.101 --> 42:02.728
I gotta report this!

42:03.270 --> 42:04.146
Wait.

42:07.191 --> 42:08.442
You'll be okay!

42:08.526 --> 42:10.152
I'm gonna go get help.

42:10.236 --> 42:13.197
Professor Ochanomizu can fix anything!

42:14.114 --> 42:15.241
There's no need.

42:15.824 --> 42:19.036
Yes, there is!
If we don't do something, you'll die!

42:19.119 --> 42:21.247
Just leave me alone.

42:21.330 --> 42:22.623
I can't!

42:23.249 --> 42:25.334
You mustn't call any humans.

42:26.460 --> 42:28.087
Then tell me what you need.

42:28.587 --> 42:30.297
What kind of energy do you use?

42:30.381 --> 42:34.301
SOL 208355.

42:34.885 --> 42:37.346
I've never heard of that one.

42:37.429 --> 42:40.307
ER 1059.

42:40.391 --> 42:42.184
Not genuine though.

42:42.268 --> 42:45.563
But it'll work as a substitute, eh?
Got it! I'll go get some!

42:45.646 --> 42:47.231
Stay where you are, okay?

42:59.034 --> 43:01.495
Are you okay?
It didn't agree with your body?

43:05.749 --> 43:06.917
Thank you.

43:07.001 --> 43:08.502
I feel better now.

43:09.086 --> 43:10.212
That's good.

43:10.879 --> 43:12.214
Mister, what's your name?

43:13.674 --> 43:14.758
I don't know.

43:15.259 --> 43:16.677
Where did you come from?

43:17.177 --> 43:18.762
I don't remember anything.

43:19.763 --> 43:21.181
All I remember is

43:21.849 --> 43:24.893
running here as hard as I could, naked...

43:24.977 --> 43:26.437
Running from something.

43:27.104 --> 43:28.939
"Running from something"?

43:30.190 --> 43:34.361
I don't know what, but it was very scary.

43:37.281 --> 43:39.450
And there was a shack over there.

43:39.533 --> 43:42.036
Must be a work shed
for the redevelopment project.

43:42.119 --> 43:44.204
I stole these clothes from there.

43:44.288 --> 43:46.332
That's why they don't fit you.

43:47.374 --> 43:48.292
You're right.

43:49.501 --> 43:52.129
You finally smiled! I'm Uran!

43:52.880 --> 43:53.922
Uran.

43:55.215 --> 43:58.052
Mister, did you paint that?

43:58.135 --> 44:00.971
Yes, there was paint in the shed.

44:01.972 --> 44:03.557
Are you an artist?

44:04.308 --> 44:05.476
I don't know.

44:05.559 --> 44:07.811
But I had the urge to make this.

44:08.395 --> 44:09.480
I know!

44:09.980 --> 44:12.274
This is called abstract painting.

44:13.025 --> 44:14.485
Abstract painting.

44:15.235 --> 44:19.073
Robots are capable of drawing
exactly what they see, right?

44:19.657 --> 44:23.035
So it's rare to see a robot
paint a picture like this!

44:24.828 --> 44:27.665
Or maybe you're just bad
at rough sketches.

44:29.249 --> 44:30.125
Maybe.

44:30.709 --> 44:33.754
I don't even know
what I was trying to depict.

44:34.463 --> 44:37.132
Or why I was doing it.

44:42.012 --> 44:43.263
I just don't know.

44:48.560 --> 44:50.479
Mister!

44:57.986 --> 44:59.029
Mister!

45:00.406 --> 45:01.990
Hello, Uran.

45:02.074 --> 45:03.367
What are you doing?

45:04.493 --> 45:05.828
Looking at these flowers.

45:06.870 --> 45:07.788
Flowers?

45:09.832 --> 45:12.501
Yesterday, there was only grass.

45:12.584 --> 45:14.795
Oh, that reminds me. I got you more!

45:15.295 --> 45:16.797
More energy catalyst!

45:16.880 --> 45:18.215
And more paints!

45:18.298 --> 45:19.299
Paints?

45:20.634 --> 45:23.011
You need more colors, don't you?

45:34.982 --> 45:38.277
Mister! I got you bigger clothes!

45:42.197 --> 45:43.532
I've finished my painting.

45:45.284 --> 45:46.118
Is this...

45:46.201 --> 45:48.495
I finally figured out what it was.

45:49.371 --> 45:50.789
A field of flowers?

45:53.917 --> 45:57.171
Your rough sketch wasn't bad at all.

45:57.838 --> 45:58.922
Actually,

46:00.090 --> 46:01.675
it brings tears to my eyes.

46:07.514 --> 46:08.849
Thank you.

46:16.523 --> 46:17.649
Uran!

46:19.443 --> 46:21.653
Good morning, Atom.

46:22.196 --> 46:24.615
Don't you think it's too early
for a "good morning"?

46:25.199 --> 46:27.910
- You think so?
- You're going again, aren't you?

46:29.161 --> 46:31.997
I found a cat, and it's so cute.

46:32.080 --> 46:34.082
An empty bottle of energy catalyst.

46:34.666 --> 46:36.418
Is this what the cat is drinking?

46:37.836 --> 46:39.546
I found it in your book bag.

46:41.965 --> 46:44.802
You searched my book bag without asking?

46:44.885 --> 46:49.097
Who went to bed right after asking me
for help with their homework?

46:50.098 --> 46:51.642
It's a robot cat.

46:51.725 --> 46:53.977
Then report it to the Ministry of Science.

46:54.061 --> 46:55.062
No!

46:55.562 --> 46:59.024
If it's broken, we should ask
Professor Ochanomizu to fix it.

46:59.566 --> 47:00.776
What's the model number?

47:01.276 --> 47:03.904
I don't know the model number.

47:03.987 --> 47:07.991
It's not made in Japan?
Which country was it made in?

47:09.201 --> 47:11.453
Anyhow, it's still scared!

47:11.954 --> 47:15.624
It's finally starting to warm up to me.
I don't want it to run away again!

47:16.124 --> 47:20.379
I'll introduce you to him
when I feel he's ready.

47:20.462 --> 47:23.257
Please don't say anything
until then, okay?

47:25.801 --> 47:28.178
Thank you! I'm off!

47:31.181 --> 47:35.102
You'll never be popular with girls
if you keep peeking in ladies' bags!

47:38.981 --> 47:40.524
Mister!

47:42.276 --> 47:44.361
Where are you, Mister?

47:45.153 --> 47:47.990
Oh no, did he really run away again?

47:50.701 --> 47:52.327
Mister!

47:52.953 --> 47:54.121
Mist-- Oh.

47:57.165 --> 48:01.712
My goodness! The clothes I gave you
are so dirty already!

48:03.213 --> 48:04.798
Hey, are you listening to me?

48:06.300 --> 48:09.761
I've finally figured out
what I was born to do.

48:09.845 --> 48:10.971
Huh?

48:11.722 --> 48:13.140
Here, look.

48:17.769 --> 48:20.105
Where did these flowers come from?

48:21.607 --> 48:22.566
Watch this.

48:39.082 --> 48:41.877
Wow, you made a dying flower bloom!

48:42.377 --> 48:43.921
What is this power?

48:44.713 --> 48:49.217
This is my... true power.

48:55.432 --> 48:57.476
So that's why you painted this picture.

48:58.268 --> 48:59.144
I'm not sure.

48:59.728 --> 49:04.107
But there was a trace of this image
in my memory.

49:04.191 --> 49:08.070
That's amazing!
You can breathe life into things!

49:09.154 --> 49:12.282
Life. Do you think we will die eventually?

49:12.991 --> 49:13.909
Die?

49:14.618 --> 49:18.205
When you saved me, you said so.

49:18.288 --> 49:20.832
That if we didn't do something,
I would die.

49:22.542 --> 49:25.379
That would mean
your computerized brain being broken.

49:25.963 --> 49:28.590
Professor Ochanomizu said
depending on how broken it is,

49:28.674 --> 49:30.217
it may be impossible to restore.

49:30.801 --> 49:33.303
Even if it's fixed,
you'd be a different robot.

49:33.387 --> 49:35.430
Is that what dying is?

49:38.183 --> 49:41.395
What does dying really mean?

49:42.312 --> 49:44.523
This flower field represents life.

49:45.107 --> 49:47.317
But there is another image.

49:48.110 --> 49:49.569
A world of death.

49:50.237 --> 49:52.030
"A world of death"?

49:52.990 --> 49:54.700
Devoid of life.

50:00.038 --> 50:02.416
What is this?

50:06.878 --> 50:09.756
What is this giant monstrosity?

50:09.840 --> 50:12.467
What is it?

50:12.551 --> 50:14.678
I'm scared!

50:14.761 --> 50:17.514
Mister! Mister, calm down!

50:24.062 --> 50:25.063
You're okay.

50:25.564 --> 50:27.107
I'm right here.

50:27.816 --> 50:29.026
No need to be afraid.

50:29.109 --> 50:29.943
It's okay.

50:30.986 --> 50:31.987
Bora.

50:32.070 --> 50:32.946
Huh?

50:34.072 --> 50:35.907
Bora.

50:36.616 --> 50:37.451
Bora?

50:44.374 --> 50:48.754
I've just arrived at Central Park,
Professor Abullah.

50:49.379 --> 50:51.715
That was quicker than I thought.

50:51.798 --> 50:54.342
You passed through customs
with no problem?

50:54.426 --> 50:55.719
<i>No problem.</i>

50:56.303 --> 50:59.931
I'm at the site
where the most recent tornado happened.

51:00.015 --> 51:03.143
I know it's a lot to ask
since the park is so big.

51:03.727 --> 51:08.106
It's no problem, sir,
because you gave me this body.

51:21.953 --> 51:26.833
When you retrieve it,
be careful not to damage it.

51:26.917 --> 51:31.046
He is another body I created, after all.

51:32.005 --> 51:35.258
<i>I'll repeat the model number
you are to retrieve.</i>

51:36.134 --> 51:40.138
<i>SOL 2083553.</i>

51:41.723 --> 51:43.642
His name is Pluto.

51:53.527 --> 51:56.404
I've located him, Professor Abullah.

51:57.197 --> 51:58.031
Good.

51:59.282 --> 52:00.992
I'm on my way.

52:01.660 --> 52:02.619
Pluto.

52:08.708 --> 52:10.293
I know you can do it, Mister!

52:10.377 --> 52:13.004
Make the whole world like this painting!

52:13.672 --> 52:15.465
"Like this painting."

52:15.549 --> 52:18.969
Yes! You can fill the world with flowers!

52:19.052 --> 52:21.429
That's why you were born.

52:22.013 --> 52:24.307
"That's why I was born."

52:24.933 --> 52:27.102
Exactly! You've got to remember.

52:27.185 --> 52:30.313
You have the power
to turn the entire world into a garden!

52:33.900 --> 52:35.318
That's not true.

52:35.861 --> 52:37.070
Not true?

52:38.321 --> 52:40.365
Not a garden.

52:40.991 --> 52:41.825
Huh?

52:43.702 --> 52:45.078
That's not it.

52:46.580 --> 52:49.708
It's something much...

52:51.126 --> 52:52.085
Yes?

52:53.211 --> 52:56.840
Much bigger. Real nature...

53:04.764 --> 53:05.849
A tornado.

53:23.491 --> 53:24.409
It's raining.

53:27.579 --> 53:28.955
Hey, look!

53:30.665 --> 53:32.792
Flowers are blooming one after the other!

53:32.876 --> 53:36.755
This is amazing!
Plants are growing so fast!

53:37.797 --> 53:39.799
It's so beautiful!

53:41.384 --> 53:42.677
Beautiful.

53:53.355 --> 53:54.564
Uran!

53:55.357 --> 53:56.983
Get away from him right now, Uran!

53:58.818 --> 54:02.113
There's a strange
electromagnetic field around him!

54:03.281 --> 54:04.115
Atom...

54:04.199 --> 54:06.868
Uran, you have to come over here now!

54:07.786 --> 54:09.579
You too, Professor Ochanomizu?

54:09.663 --> 54:12.958
I've asked the staff
from the Ministry of Science to come!

54:15.669 --> 54:18.463
I can't believe you, Atom!
You promised you wouldn't tell!

54:18.546 --> 54:21.258
Now is not the time for that!

54:21.341 --> 54:23.385
There's something dangerous
about that robot!

54:25.262 --> 54:26.721
Squad A, in position!

54:27.722 --> 54:29.766
- Squad B, in position!
- What?

54:30.433 --> 54:31.476
The police too?

54:32.060 --> 54:34.688
- Professor?
- Who told you to call the police?

54:35.814 --> 54:38.275
I reported it per regulations.

54:41.236 --> 54:43.863
Inspector Nakamura of the police!
Are you all right?

54:43.947 --> 54:45.282
How could you?

54:45.824 --> 54:48.326
How could you do this, Atom?

54:49.411 --> 54:50.787
Atom.

54:50.870 --> 54:52.998
You've got to get over here now, Uran!

54:54.207 --> 54:55.959
Atom.

55:05.927 --> 55:07.304
Atom.

55:11.099 --> 55:12.350
Hatred.

55:13.893 --> 55:17.522
System... overload...

55:17.605 --> 55:20.358
Stop! Stop, or we'll shoot!

55:20.442 --> 55:21.609
Mister...

55:27.032 --> 55:28.616
I'm going to explode!

55:32.037 --> 55:34.039
The surge

55:34.622 --> 55:36.207
of rage...

55:37.334 --> 55:38.418
Fire!

55:38.501 --> 55:39.461
Wait!

55:42.130 --> 55:44.174
So many robots...

55:44.716 --> 55:45.925
Death...

55:48.970 --> 55:52.390
They deserve to die.

55:52.474 --> 55:54.851
How many did I...

55:57.687 --> 55:58.855
kill?

56:00.106 --> 56:03.234
Flowers in the desert...

56:05.987 --> 56:08.323
A world of death.

56:14.704 --> 56:15.580
Horns!

56:21.378 --> 56:22.670
Mister!

56:30.595 --> 56:32.389
I don't believe this!

56:33.223 --> 56:34.891
What's the matter, Professor?

56:35.767 --> 56:37.352
This can't be.

56:38.228 --> 56:40.814
His computerized brain is missing!

56:53.785 --> 56:55.370
What was that?

56:55.453 --> 56:57.330
Oh, there it is!

56:59.541 --> 57:01.584
That's my body!

57:02.752 --> 57:04.003
What?

57:05.296 --> 57:10.510
I'm a construction robot
working at this redevelopment site.

57:11.136 --> 57:11.970
Huh?

57:12.053 --> 57:15.515
I finished my 100-hour shift,
and when I was ready to go home,

57:15.598 --> 57:18.476
I saw that my off-duty body was missing.

57:18.560 --> 57:22.355
So, this is your body?

57:22.439 --> 57:26.651
I've been looking for it.
I'm so glad I found it!

57:28.653 --> 57:30.572
What on earth is going on?

57:32.115 --> 57:34.367
A robot
without its artificial intelligence...

57:37.287 --> 57:38.746
somehow activated on its own?

57:53.553 --> 57:54.804
It's right over here.

57:55.638 --> 57:59.017
Calling it "wandering anima"
makes it sound dignified,

57:59.517 --> 58:02.103
but it is only a robot
without a computerized brain,

58:02.187 --> 58:04.772
remotely controlled
through electromagnetic waves.

58:05.773 --> 58:08.735
Are you satisfied now?
The time for your little stroll is over.

58:10.778 --> 58:12.363
Come back.

58:16.451 --> 58:20.163
This is your only body, Pluto.

58:32.842 --> 58:34.928
And don't forget your orders

58:35.887 --> 58:36.846
<i>to kill Atom.</i>

01:01:13.211 --> 01:01:16.881
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
